From 1c06a3e1e37d53b7a48d3e27708eb8b2b0190f27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:05:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): refuse a bore dwell where G86 has no dwell
 word; pin G86 per post (#1445)

The Fanuc-family posts and sinumerik wrote P<ms> on G86. The published
Fanuc and Haas G86 formats have no P word, so the control dropped the
dwell without a message. These posts now refuse a bore with a dwell by
name. tormach and grblhal keep G86 P<seconds> (LinuxCNC form). A bore
with no dwell posts as before; no existing golden changes.

A drilling dwell outside 0..3600 s is refused by name in
CreateOperation and EditOperationParams (and so MCP edit_operation).

Pinned by crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs (new goldens in
tests/golden/bore/) and crates/app/tests/bore_cycle.rs.

Refs #1445

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
